WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:04.791
Cleo watched the sun set behind the hills.

2
00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:08.812
The final round of the contest was about to begin.

3
00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:12.330
She and Roscoe were tied.

4
00:00:12.331 --> 00:00:17.281
"A good sheriff can track down outlaws," Fritzy said.

5
00:00:17.282 --> 00:00:21.844
"Our friend Zeke is pretending to be an outlaw.

6
00:00:21.845 --> 00:00:24.894
He's hiding in those hills.

7
00:00:24.895 --> 00:00:30.469
Whoever finds him is our new sheriff."

8
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:34.753
"Can we do this tomorrow?" Cleo asked.

9
00:00:34.754 --> 00:00:37.646
"It's getting dark."

10
00:00:37.647 --> 00:00:43.741
Roscoe snorted. "Sheriffs work whenever they have to."

11
00:00:43.742 --> 00:00:49.397
"Right," Cleo said. "I was just kidding!"

12
00:00:49.398 --> 00:00:55.206
She gulped. "Roscoe is going to win," she thought.

13
00:00:55.207 --> 00:01:00.280
"And I'll go to jail!"

14
00:01:00.281 --> 00:01:03.884
Roscoe and Cleo rode out of town.

15
00:01:03.885 --> 00:01:07.533
Roscoe felt a knot in his belly.

16
00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:10.457
What if Cleo won?

17
00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:14.584
The folks in Prickly Pear seemed to like her.

18
00:01:14.585 --> 00:01:16.844
But it wasn't right!

19
00:01:16.845 --> 00:01:21.122
That cat was a thief!

20
00:01:21.123 --> 00:01:24.948
Roscoe kept looking at the ground.

21
00:01:24.949 --> 00:01:28.180
Cleo gave him a funny look.

22
00:01:28.181 --> 00:01:31.002
"Why are you looking down?"

23
00:01:31.003 --> 00:01:34.735
"I'm looking for tracks," he said.

24
00:01:34.736 --> 00:01:40.417
"Oh," Cleo said. "That's a good idea."

25
00:01:40.418 --> 00:01:43.306
"Mm-hmm," Roscoe snapped.

26
00:01:43.307 --> 00:01:47.421
"That's why I'm the real sheriff."

27
00:01:47.422 --> 00:01:50.474
They rode for a bit longer.

28
00:01:50.475 --> 00:01:55.047
Then Cleo gasped.

29
00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.105
"Hoofprints! Lots of them!

30
00:01:58.106 --> 00:02:01.653
So long, Roscoe! Ha-ha!"

31
00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.794
She took off.

32
00:02:03.795 --> 00:02:06.550
Roscoe looked at the tracks.

33
00:02:06.551 --> 00:02:10.481
"Those are from several horses," he thought.

34
00:02:10.482 --> 00:02:18.052
"But Zeke probably has only one horse."

35
00:02:18.053 --> 00:02:21.586
He soon found another set of hoofprints.

36
00:02:21.587 --> 00:02:29.342
They were from one horse.

37
00:02:29.343 --> 00:02:33.687
He followed them up a hill.

38
00:02:33.688 --> 00:02:38.840
"Ugh." Cleo stopped near a tree stump.

39
00:02:38.841 --> 00:02:41.397
"I don't see any more tracks.

40
00:02:41.398 --> 00:02:43.075
But I can't turn back.

41
00:02:43.076 --> 00:02:45.495
I have to find Zeke.

42
00:02:45.496 --> 00:02:48.922
If I don't, I'll go to jail."

43
00:02:48.923 --> 00:02:56.335
She found a trail and followed it.

44
00:02:56.336 --> 00:03:01.911
The trail went on and on.

45
00:03:01.912 --> 00:03:05.544
Soon she saw a tree stump.

46
00:03:05.545 --> 00:03:11.823
Cleo groaned. "It's the same one!

47
00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:19.717
I'm going in circles!" She took a breath.

48
00:03:19.718 --> 00:03:22.236
"Maybe I should head back to town.

49
00:03:22.237 --> 00:03:25.557
I'm never going to . . ."

50
00:03:25.558 --> 00:03:31.945
Just then a campfire flickered on a nearby hilltop.

51
00:03:31.946 --> 00:03:39.440
Cleo grinned. "That must be Zeke!"

52
00:03:39.441 --> 00:03:44.684
Roscoe stopped his horse and sniffed.

53
00:03:44.685 --> 00:03:50.454
"Someone's cooking," he thought. "It must be Zeke!"

54
00:03:50.455 --> 00:03:52.952
He followed the scent.

55
00:03:52.953 --> 00:03:57.741
Soon he saw a campfire on a hilltop.

56
00:03:57.742 --> 00:04:01.377
Roscoe rode up to the site.

57
00:04:01.378 --> 00:04:05.519
A toad was cooking beans.

58
00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.664
"You found me," the toad said. "I'm Zeke."

59
00:04:10.665 --> 00:04:14.612
"Phew." Roscoe sighed with relief.

60
00:04:14.613 --> 00:04:17.582
"And I'm the sheriff!"

61
00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:19.936
Cleo rode fast.

62
00:04:19.937 --> 00:04:23.101
She could smell the campfire.

63
00:04:23.102 --> 00:04:29.965
"It looks like I'll be the sheriff." She laughed.

64
00:04:29.966 --> 00:04:36.045
"Maybe I can put Roscoe in jail! Ha-ha!"

65
00:04:36.046 --> 00:04:39.296
She reached the hilltop.

66
00:04:39.297 --> 00:04:44.544
Then she stopped laughing.

67
00:04:44.545 --> 00:04:54.655
Three nasty-looking wolves were aiming slingshots at her!

